        "outcome": "local",
        "answer": "According to the context, the budget veto works as follows:\n\n1. A `RoutingGate` decides which tier answers a request.\n2. A rolling window budget is applied to the decision.\n3. If the budget is insufficient, the decision is vetoed and logged as `degraded_local` in the budget ledger.\n4. The veto is recorded and can be replayed later to verify the decision.\n5. The veto is authoritative, meaning it cannot be silently ignored or overwritten.\n\nIn other words, the budget veto ensures that the cloud quota is only spent on work that a local model cannot do, and provides a way to prove afterwards which decisions were made and which were vetoed due to budget constraints.",
